# Vesuva enters as a copy of a Mutavault that is a 2/2 creature until end of turn: the animation is not a copy effect, so it
# is no copiable value (CR 707.2; the ruling: no "non-copy effects that changed its types"). The Vesuva-Mutavault is a Land
# and no creature, with no power or toughness, while the original stays a Land Creature. (The Mutavault pays its own {1}.)

[Bot1 Deck]
Mutavault
Vesuva
Forest x13

[Bot2 Deck]
Island x15

[Actions]
Bot1.Hand.Mutavault.Play
[T3 Bot1.Main1]
Bot1.Battlefield.Mutavault.Activate(Ability: becomes)
Bot1.Battlefield.Mutavault.Activate(Ability: {C})
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Pass
? Bot1.Battlefield.Mutavault.Types = Land; Creature
Bot1.Hand.Vesuva.Play
Bot1.Accept
Bot1.Pass

[Expect]
Bot1.Battlefield = Mutavault; Mutavault
Bot1.Battlefield.Mutavault#1.Types = Land; Creature
Bot1.Battlefield.Mutavault#1.Power = 2
Bot1.Battlefield.Mutavault#2.Types = Land
Bot1.Battlefield.Mutavault#2.Power = (absent)
Bot1.Battlefield.Mutavault#2.Tapped = true
